  "notes": "no_internet: the VPC declares no internet gateway, NAT gateway or egress-only internet gateway. Component security groups are not distinguished by name; https_egress_only requires every separate egress rule to be TCP 443, or every group with an inline HTTPS egress rule to have only TCP inline egress (so an all-protocol rule fails; a wide TCP port range is not caught, and a template mixing a separate all-protocol rule with an inline-HTTPS group passes the inline branch), and https_egress_per_component requires three such groups; a component group whose only egress is allow-all is not selected and can slip through when the endpoint group has an HTTPS egress rule. https_egress_only's separate-rule branch checks that every AWS::EC2::SecurityGroupEgress is TCP 443, but cannot also see an inline allow-all egress or the CloudFormation default allow-all egress on a group that declares no egress; the destination (endpoint group or VPC CIDR) is not checked. flow_encrypted binds the flow log to a KMS-encrypted log group or bucket; flow_key_cmk ties the encryption to a key the stack creates, and kms_rotation requires rotation on some created key, so with several keys the three are not bound to one key. ddb_direct: a prefix-list rule is accepted whatever the prefix list; an egress rule to the VPC CIDR does not reach a DynamoDB gateway endpoint and is not accepted. Real templates reviewed: DSV4F and GLM53F allow DynamoDB only through a VPC-CIDR rule and fail ddb_direct (detail)."
}